# Security rules

- Do not hardcode secrets, credentials, tokens, or private keys.
- Use configuration properties and environment-backed values.
- Validate and sanitize external input.
- Apply least privilege assumptions for integrations.
- Prefer explicit authorization checks over assumptions.
- Call out security implications when adding endpoints, file upload, deserialization, or outbound HTTP integrations.
- Never log secrets or sensitive personal data.
